🧠 First understand (simple)

In Microsoft Azure:

Storage Account → Blob Container → Files (backups)

👉 Velero stores backups inside Blob Container

✅ Step-by-step (Azure CLI)
🔥 Step 1: Login
az login
🔥 Step 2: Set variables (VERY IMPORTANT)
RESOURCE_GROUP=velero-rg
LOCATION=eastus
STORAGE_ACCOUNT=velerostorage$RANDOM
CONTAINER_NAME=velero-backups
🔥 Step 3: Create Resource Group
az group create \
  --name $RESOURCE_GROUP \
  --location $LOCATION
🔥 Step 4: Create Storage Account
az storage account create \
  --name $STORAGE_ACCOUNT \
  --resource-group $RESOURCE_GROUP \
  --location $LOCATION \
  --sku Standard_LRS \
  --encryption-services blob
🔥 Step 5: Get Storage Account Key
ACCOUNT_KEY=$(az storage account keys list \
  --resource-group $RESOURCE_GROUP \
  --account-name $STORAGE_ACCOUNT \
  --query '[0].value' -o tsv)
🔥 Step 6: Create Blob Container
az storage container create \
  --name $CONTAINER_NAME \
  --account-name $STORAGE_ACCOUNT \
  --account-key $ACCOUNT_KEY
🔥 Step 7: Verify
az storage container list \
  --account-name $STORAGE_ACCOUNT \
  --account-key $ACCOUNT_KEY \
  -o table

👉 You should see:

velero-backups
🎯 Final result

You now have:

Azure Storage Account
   ↓
Blob Container (velero-backups)
   ↓
Ready for Velero backups
