👉 Keep backups only for last 7 days
👉 Older backups → automatically deleted

🧠 How Velero does this
Velero uses something called:

TTL (Time To Live)


⏰ Example
TTL = 168h  → 168 hours = 7 days

✅ 1. While creating backup (manual)
velero backup create nginx-backup \  --ttl 168h
👉 After 7 days → backup auto deleted

✅ 2. BEST WAY (Production) → Use schedule
Instead of manual backup, companies use scheduled backups

🔥 Daily backup + keep only 7 days
velero schedule create daily-backup \  --schedule="0 2 * * *" \  --ttl 168h

🧠 What this does


Runs every day at 2 AM


Keeps backup for 7 days


Old backups auto removed



📅 How it works internally
Day 1 → Backup1Day 2 → Backup2...Day 7 → Backup7Day 8 → Backup1 deleted ❌

🔍 Check schedules
velero schedule get

🔍 Check backups
velero backup get

🧠 Production best practice

✅ 1. Always use schedule (not manual)
Manual = ❌
Scheduled = ✅

✅ 2. Different TTL for different environments
EnvironmentTTLDev2–3 daysStaging7 daysProduction15–30 days

✅ 3. Use labels (advanced)
velero backup create prod-backup \  --ttl 168h \  --labels env=prod

✅ 4. Monitor backups
👉 If backup fails → alert

